   "harm": "unclear terminology around attributable outputs confuses RPC documentation and code",
   "hash": "af1d3d9b448a2379",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:27:14+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3590893562",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3590893562",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "The \"cannot be attributed\" here also confuses me. FWIU at this point in the review, when no outputs go to ourselves, or all outputs go ourselves, we consider it \"attributable\", but if there are both foreign-owned inputs and foreign-owned outputs, we call it \"not attributable\". If that\u2019s the correct understanding, perhaps we can find a more speaking description of that?",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34872#discussion_r3590893562"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-07-15",
   "author": "murchandamus",
   "author_replies": [],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "spent TXO values should always be known from the UTXO set or block undo data, making the assumption of unknown foreign input values questionable",
   "hash": "b3c8a02e1ae217d6",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:27:14+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3591065461",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3591065461",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "The \"known zero value\" keeps throwing me for a loop. Transactions can only spend TXOs that are in our UTXO set when we first see them. Therefore, we should always know every spent TXO\u2019s value when we first validate a transaction.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34872#discussion_r3591065461"
  }
 ],
